    "insights": [
      "Uniqueness-by-recurrence: the Gamma closed form is a fixed point of the same 2-step recurrence with the same base data (a2=2/pi, a3=1/2), so equality follows by induction without evaluating the sphere-average integral.",
      "The recurrence gammaForm(k+2)=(k/(k+1))*gammaForm(k) collapses to a single field_simp once Gamma((k+2)/2)=(k/2)Gamma(k/2) and Gamma((k+3)/2)=((k+1)/2)Gamma((k+1)/2) are applied via Real.Gamma_add_one.",
      "Base cases use only Gamma(1/2)=sqrt(pi) and Gamma(1)=1; even/odd rational-vs-pi dichotomy traces to these.",
